WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.020 --> 00:02.100
[The D Dorm]

3
00:05.320 --> 00:06.530
How ironic that

4
00:06.910 --> 00:09.860
we searched the entire dorm for Grandma Gaysorn's relative,

5
00:09.930 --> 00:12.410
only for the photo to come from Ms. Danis.

6
00:12.430 --> 00:15.130
This is straight out of a one31 evening drama.

7
00:15.710 --> 00:17.010
- How so? - Well...

8
00:17.330 --> 00:19.450
it's that plot where parents look for their missing child.

9
00:19.480 --> 00:21.500
Or the child is searching for their parents.

10
00:21.520 --> 00:22.940
They kept missing each other.

11
00:23.020 --> 00:24.540
They almost met, yet never did.

12
00:24.560 --> 00:25.570
Oh, in some dramas,

13
00:25.600 --> 00:29.780
a blind father has to search for his missing wife and child.

14
00:29.800 --> 00:32.130
Yeah, I really love that kinda plot.

15
00:32.150 --> 00:33.590
I've always wanted to give that role a try.

16
00:37.340 --> 00:38.310
My child.

17
00:38.440 --> 00:39.140
Dear.

18
00:39.160 --> 00:39.820
Hey.

19
00:39.830 --> 00:40.970
- Hey... - Whoa.

20
00:40.980 --> 00:41.860
Hey.

21
00:42.230 --> 00:43.230
Hey,

22
00:43.870 --> 00:45.420
is this my child?

23
00:45.440 --> 00:46.730
How did you grow up

24
00:46.800 --> 00:48.530
to have skin as bumpy as the Moon's, dear?

25
00:48.550 --> 00:49.450
Ugh!

26
00:50.220 --> 00:51.740
Why are you playing along with him?

27
00:53.020 --> 00:53.810
Ugh...

28
00:55.020 --> 00:56.300
Where's Ms. Danis?

29
00:56.480 --> 00:57.520
Why isn't she here yet?

30
00:57.740 --> 00:58.740
Her phone was dead when I called.

31
00:58.760 --> 00:59.780
I didn't even get to talk to her.

32
01:00.610 --> 01:02.140
I’ll go check for you.

33
01:05.330 --> 01:07.180
There are no cars in the parking lot.

34
01:07.270 --> 01:09.330
Maybe she is coming here by taxi.

35
01:12.980 --> 01:15.830
Maybe she parked under the dorm.

36
01:16.330 --> 01:17.340
Ugh!

37
01:17.410 --> 01:17.980
What?

38
01:18.000 --> 01:19.539
Stop popping in and out already.

39
01:19.560 --> 01:20.510
I'm dizzy.

40
01:22.539 --> 01:23.300
Oh!

41
01:26.340 --> 01:27.340
I meant,

42
01:27.840 --> 01:31.120
I've been going back and forth trying to picture

43
01:31.140 --> 01:32.390
what Grandma Gaysorn looks like,

44
01:32.570 --> 01:34.660
and it's making me dizzy.

45
01:34.680 --> 01:35.880
- I see. - Yes.

46
01:35.900 --> 01:37.340
So that's how it is.

47
01:37.530 --> 01:38.640
Hey, Dobby.

48
01:38.650 --> 01:39.120
Huh?

49
01:39.130 --> 01:41.210
When you talked to Danis,

50
01:41.340 --> 01:43.000
she said that the box she was carrying

51
01:43.020 --> 01:44.410
belonged to the director of the orphanage.

52
01:44.810 --> 01:45.880
Is there a chance

53
01:46.060 --> 01:48.220
that the orphanage director is Grandma Gaysorn?

54
01:49.979 --> 01:51.020
I do not think so.

55
01:51.390 --> 01:52.539
She said that

56
01:52.920 --> 01:54.700
the director's name was Nampetch.

57
01:56.620 --> 01:58.810
Her orphanage director is named Nampetch.

58
01:59.920 --> 02:01.030
Where?

59
02:01.330 --> 02:02.680
Where is Grandma Gaysorn's photo?

60
02:02.710 --> 02:04.610
Let me see the photo you said I dropped.

61
02:04.630 --> 02:05.410
Here.

62
02:07.430 --> 02:08.259
Huh?

63
02:08.340 --> 02:10.639
Is this the photo? I can't even see her face.

64
02:10.660 --> 02:11.740
You don't remember?

65
02:11.760 --> 02:12.760
Hey,

66
02:13.120 --> 02:15.340
are you sure I was the one who dropped this?

67
02:15.360 --> 02:17.110
Mr. Disney told me that

68
02:17.329 --> 02:19.140
as he was walking up to the fourth floor,

69
02:19.170 --> 02:21.060
this was the photo

70
02:21.070 --> 02:22.180
that fell past him.

71
02:22.630 --> 02:25.500
When he got to the fourth floor, he saw you carrying a cardboard box,

72
02:26.140 --> 02:27.540
so you probably dropped it.

73
02:27.560 --> 02:29.220
Hey, Ms. Danis, I think...

74
02:29.240 --> 02:30.620
you should call the director

75
02:30.640 --> 02:32.660
and ask her if this photo is hers.

76
02:35.930 --> 02:37.520
It's probably too late to call her now.

77
02:37.540 --> 02:38.190
- Huh? - Huh?

78
02:40.630 --> 02:41.630
Don't tell me...

79
02:42.060 --> 02:43.180
Did she pass away?

80
02:44.740 --> 02:45.530
She already went to bed.

81
02:45.550 --> 02:46.430
- Oh. - Ugh.

82
02:46.900 --> 02:48.500
Then why did you look so worried?

83
02:48.740 --> 02:49.850
Well, even if she's awake,

84
02:49.870 --> 02:51.910
she wouldn't be able to give you any answers.

85
02:52.110 --> 02:52.930
Huh?

86
02:52.960 --> 02:55.530
Lately, I've been visiting her more often

87
02:56.130 --> 02:57.420
because she has Alzheimer's disease.

88
02:57.440 --> 02:58.700
She can't remember much.

89
02:58.720 --> 02:59.530
Oh...

90
03:00.140 --> 03:01.140
See?

91
03:01.340 --> 03:03.340
This is definitely a one31 evening drama plot.

92
03:03.620 --> 03:05.940
She has memory loss due to Alzheimer's disease.

93
03:05.960 --> 03:08.370
Given the chance, I'd like to work with Boyd Kosiyabong.

94
03:09.010 --> 03:10.010
Boy Takonkiet.

95
03:10.320 --> 03:11.840
I have to get this role.

96
03:12.630 --> 03:13.720
My child.

97
03:14.000 --> 03:14.820
Dear.

98
03:14.980 --> 03:16.800
Hey, why did you grow up

99
03:16.820 --> 03:18.770
to be so shameless, sweetheart?

100
03:18.800 --> 03:19.690
Ugh!

101
03:20.030 --> 03:22.260
Stop touching my face already, you Grade B supporting actor.

102
03:22.410 --> 03:23.490
Whoa, that's harsh.

103
03:25.480 --> 03:26.140
Hey,

104
03:26.230 --> 03:27.460
we have to talk to the director

105
03:27.620 --> 03:29.210
in case she knows Grandma Gaysorn.

106
03:31.500 --> 03:33.010
Ugh!

107
03:33.030 --> 03:35.300
Why is our meeting

108
03:35.630 --> 03:38.390
so full of obstacles?!

109
03:38.810 --> 03:42.720
"It is as if the heavens are tormenting us.

110
03:43.420 --> 03:47.900
With no way out of this anguish, put up with it we musk.

111
03:47.920 --> 03:52.010
It is not easy to improvise poems, you see?

112
03:52.700 --> 03:57.130
Writer's block has befallen me. Oh, how I wish to be free."

113
03:58.140 --> 04:00.630
Gaysorn, where are you?!

114
04:11.210 --> 04:14.760
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

115
04:14.780 --> 04:18.560
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

116
04:21.110 --> 04:26.860
♫Every step we take has a meaning♫

117
04:28.220 --> 04:32.980
♫No path is ever meaningless♫

118
04:35.300 --> 04:41.540
♫As long as our hearts keep searching♫

119
04:42.520 --> 04:46.980
♫One day, we'll find what we're yearning for♫

120
04:46.980 --> 04:50.630
♫Walking alone is fine, but it's better when you're by my side♫

121
04:50.630 --> 04:54.220
♫It won't be lonely when you're here to walk beside♫

122
04:54.220 --> 04:57.140
♫Like a love that waits, waits at the D Dorm♫

123
04:57.790 --> 05:00.270
♫Like a love that remains, remains at the dorm♫

124
05:00.270 --> 05:06.730
♫Meaningful love and good things await on every path♫

125
05:07.170 --> 05:13.850
♫It might not be a coincidence that we get to meet♫

126
05:14.370 --> 05:21.520
♫There might be hidden meanings on the path beneath our feet♫

127
05:21.540 --> 05:28.770
♫Perhaps the D Dorm is what led me to meet you♫

128
05:28.800 --> 05:32.580
[The D Dorm]

129
05:32.590 --> 05:34.150
[The D Dorm]

130
05:34.320 --> 05:35.700
Oh, where's Handyman Daeng?

131
05:35.720 --> 05:37.420
Didn't he say he'd go to the nursing home with us?

132
05:37.440 --> 05:39.300
Oh, he went to get some coffee at Mr. Drip's cafe.

133
05:39.640 --> 05:40.409
I see.

134
05:40.430 --> 05:41.120
Oh, there he is.

135
05:41.140 --> 05:41.670
Oh.

136
05:43.820 --> 05:45.500
Hey, what is he carrying?

137
05:48.420 --> 05:49.420
Okay.

138
05:50.240 --> 05:51.350
I'm ready...

139
05:52.120 --> 05:53.310
Whoa.

140
05:53.330 --> 05:54.420
Look at you.

141
05:54.720 --> 05:56.260
Were you up all night or something?

142
05:56.430 --> 05:57.620
Last night,

143
05:58.030 --> 06:00.420
Dawin had me holding his hand

144
06:00.450 --> 06:02.000
while we looked for Gramps' ghost all night.

145
06:02.020 --> 06:03.020
Until 5 A.M.

146
06:04.060 --> 06:06.460
Wow, you two used to fight all the time,

147
06:06.610 --> 06:11.450
but now you're walking around holding hands all night, huh?

148
06:12.460 --> 06:13.330
Oops...

149
06:13.770 --> 06:15.220
You're getting mad over just a little teasing?

150
06:16.950 --> 06:17.940
- Whoa! - Whoa!

151
06:17.960 --> 06:18.600
I'm good, I'm good!

152
06:18.610 --> 06:20.720
All good, all good, all good...

153
06:20.740 --> 06:21.940
Daeng, you're falling asleep standing up.

154
06:21.950 --> 06:23.020
Why don't you go to bed?

155
06:35.510 --> 06:36.909
Alright, I'm ready.

156
06:38.159 --> 06:38.870
Hey,

157
06:38.880 --> 06:40.330
don't get your hopes up.

158
06:40.350 --> 06:41.480
To be honest,

159
06:41.500 --> 06:43.970
I'm not even sure if she'll remember anything.

160
06:43.990 --> 06:45.190
She even mistook me

161
06:45.320 --> 06:47.380
for a friend her age.

162
06:47.610 --> 06:48.610
Hm...

163
06:48.630 --> 06:49.900
Maybe it's because you look old?

164
06:50.430 --> 06:53.630
Yeah? You asking for an earful, huh?

165
06:54.120 --> 06:55.940
I was...reading Guard Dum's thoughts.

166
06:55.970 --> 06:57.140
Guard Dum, were you thinking out loud?

167
06:57.300 --> 06:59.220
Your mother looks young enough to be your age.

168
06:59.810 --> 07:00.810
That's right.

169
07:01.120 --> 07:02.180
Let's say

170
07:02.420 --> 07:03.920
the OD doesn't remember anything...

171
07:03.940 --> 07:04.630
Hm?

172
07:04.780 --> 07:05.780
- What's "OD"? - Who's that?

173
07:06.530 --> 07:07.420
The orphanage director.

174
07:07.710 --> 07:08.850
- Oh. - I see.

175
07:08.870 --> 07:11.300
How are we gonna find Grandma Gaysorn after this?

176
07:14.390 --> 07:16.330
I guess I'll have to light some incense and tell Grandpa

177
07:16.690 --> 07:19.270
to let go and reincarnate already.

178
07:21.320 --> 07:22.940
I do not want to!

179
07:22.960 --> 07:24.820
I am not going anywhere.

180
07:24.840 --> 07:26.820
You have to find Gaysorn.

181
07:26.840 --> 07:29.100
If you do not find her,

182
07:29.120 --> 07:32.650
I will stick to you like a tick on a dog forever.

183
07:32.920 --> 07:34.830
Whoa.

184
07:36.140 --> 07:37.310
Hello.

185
07:37.530 --> 07:38.730
We're on our way.

186
07:39.830 --> 07:41.210
- Huh?! - Hm? Huh? Huh?

187
07:41.520 --> 07:42.820
I'll be right there!

188
07:43.220 --> 07:44.409
Alright, yes.

189
07:45.340 --> 07:46.740
Her caregiver called

190
07:47.020 --> 07:48.230
and said my mother had disappeared.

191
07:48.520 --> 07:50.300
They looked everywhere but couldn't find her.

192
07:50.520 --> 07:51.620
Hey, calm down.

193
07:51.840 --> 07:52.920
She's quite old,

194
07:53.420 --> 07:54.270
so she can't have gone far.

195
07:54.370 --> 07:55.320
We'll help you look for her.

196
07:55.460 --> 07:57.180
How about this? Go report it to the police first.

197
07:57.420 --> 07:59.610
I'll wait for Dax, then join you in the search.

198
08:00.110 --> 08:00.820
Sounds good?

199
08:01.000 --> 08:01.750
Okay.

200
08:01.770 --> 08:03.500
- Let's go. - Go, go, go, go.

201
08:03.520 --> 08:05.220
- Ugh! Come on, Guard Dum. - Mm, that guy's still asleep.

202
08:05.240 --> 08:06.630
Daeng, come on!

203
08:06.650 --> 08:07.330
Hurry.

204
08:07.860 --> 08:09.740
♫Daeng is a fighter♫

205
08:10.460 --> 08:11.210
Ugh...

206
08:12.430 --> 08:14.180
Ugh...what's taking him so long?!

207
08:14.200 --> 08:15.000
It is already this late.

208
08:15.020 --> 08:16.510
Oh, here he is.

209
08:17.730 --> 08:18.490
So?

210
08:18.510 --> 08:19.250
Sorry, sorry.

211
08:19.270 --> 08:21.210
I was looking for a way to help the director regain her memory.

212
08:21.340 --> 08:22.260
I found a way

213
08:22.430 --> 08:23.220
thanks to the Ex.

214
08:23.320 --> 08:24.230
Expert?

215
08:24.250 --> 08:25.080
Extension cord.

216
08:25.760 --> 08:26.350
It actually works.

217
08:26.360 --> 08:28.060
After I took a shower this morning,

218
08:28.080 --> 08:28.860
I got an electric shock

219
08:28.880 --> 08:30.460
when I plugged in my hair dryer to blow-dry my hair.

220
08:30.480 --> 08:32.539
Memories came rushing back to me.

221
08:32.559 --> 08:33.789
My dad's and my mom's faces

222
08:33.820 --> 08:35.260
flashed...through my mind.

223
08:35.289 --> 08:37.740
Oh, so you'll shock the director with that extension cord.

224
08:37.760 --> 08:39.220
Yes, in case Grandma Gaysorn's face

225
08:39.240 --> 08:41.130
appears... in her memories, too.

226
08:41.150 --> 08:43.370
It appears...you might be sent to jail.

227
08:43.390 --> 08:44.620
Are you crazy?

228
08:44.820 --> 08:46.420
Get in the car. Everyone's already left.

229
08:46.440 --> 08:47.030
Hurry!

230
08:48.180 --> 08:48.980
Oh...

231
08:49.040 --> 08:50.100
Wait.

232
09:01.580 --> 09:04.500
[Dohyun, occupation: Korean fortune teller]

233
09:04.730 --> 09:07.260
Why is this ice cream seller dressed like that?

234
09:07.420 --> 09:09.230
It is like he is from the Joseon era.

235
09:09.330 --> 09:11.580
I have cleansed all the negative energy, Mr. Delta.

236
09:20.530 --> 09:23.430
[Delta, occupation: businessman]

237
09:23.940 --> 09:24.940
Stop!

238
09:25.640 --> 09:28.300
Mr. Delta, since this is our first visit to your new business,

239
09:28.980 --> 09:30.420
you must always step in

240
09:30.440 --> 09:32.060
with your left foot first for good luck.

241
09:33.550 --> 09:35.220
- Tank you... - Hey!

242
09:35.240 --> 09:35.860
That is my rhrine.

243
09:36.010 --> 09:37.230
Thank you for warning me, Dohyun.

244
09:44.950 --> 09:46.480
- Whoa... - Oh... The way he walks.

245
09:46.550 --> 09:47.690
Hello, Mr. Dobby.

246
09:49.320 --> 09:50.780
Do we...know each other?

247
09:50.930 --> 09:52.820
My name is Delta.

248
09:53.230 --> 09:55.860
My father is the one who's going to buy this dorm from you.

249
09:56.540 --> 09:57.540
I see.

250
09:58.020 --> 09:58.820
And this is

251
09:59.020 --> 09:59.780
Dohyun,

252
09:59.800 --> 10:00.910
my personal fortune teller.

253
10:01.330 --> 10:01.900
Herro.

254
10:01.920 --> 10:02.920
What halo? I'm not dead.

255
10:04.020 --> 10:05.300
What can I do for you, Mr. Delta?

256
10:05.320 --> 10:06.820
My fortune teller said

257
10:07.210 --> 10:09.540
my auspicious item is here in this dorm.

258
10:09.930 --> 10:12.670
That's why I came here to look for it.

259
10:12.690 --> 10:13.540
Uh...

260
10:13.560 --> 10:14.480
Could you come another day?

261
10:14.500 --> 10:15.730
He cannot!

262
10:17.440 --> 10:18.610
Hey, he's acting crazy.

263
10:20.020 --> 10:20.950
Tomorrow

264
10:21.120 --> 10:23.220
is the Sacred Phoenix's birthday!

265
10:23.620 --> 10:24.600
Mr. Delta

266
10:24.610 --> 10:27.810
will have to find everyone who possesses a piece of the phoenix.

267
10:28.120 --> 10:29.740
Right now, he already has the head,

268
10:29.930 --> 10:30.620
shoulders,

269
10:30.810 --> 10:31.410
- Knees. - knees.

270
10:31.430 --> 10:31.970
- Hey! - Hey!

271
10:32.660 --> 10:33.930
I wanted to say that

272
10:34.030 --> 10:35.390
the shoulder part is unnecessary.

273
10:35.410 --> 10:36.720
Do Koreans know this joke, too?

274
10:36.750 --> 10:37.550
I just found that out, too.

275
10:38.310 --> 10:39.260
What are the body parts?

276
10:39.520 --> 10:40.820
There have to be a head,

277
10:41.320 --> 10:42.590
- wings, - Wings.

278
10:42.610 --> 10:44.150
- a tail, - A tail.

279
10:44.170 --> 10:45.390
- and claws. - Claws.

280
10:45.410 --> 10:47.530
There is only one part missing.

281
10:47.550 --> 10:48.380
That is...

282
10:48.400 --> 10:48.920
The heart?

283
10:48.940 --> 10:49.600
The appendix.

284
10:49.620 --> 10:50.350
- Huh? - Hm?

285
10:50.620 --> 10:51.620
Why is the appendix crucial?

286
10:51.720 --> 10:53.070
The appendix is an extra part.

287
10:53.090 --> 10:54.860
The symbol of imperfection.

288
10:54.880 --> 10:56.090
Yet it is needed.

289
10:57.310 --> 10:59.820
Just as there is yin, there must be yang.

290
10:59.920 --> 11:01.520
The appendix maintains the balance.

291
11:02.740 --> 11:03.820
Let's not waste our time, Dohyun.

292
11:04.660 --> 11:06.580
Let's go find the phoenix's appendix.

293
11:06.620 --> 11:07.240
Yes.

294
11:12.460 --> 11:13.740
Whoa!

295
11:15.220 --> 11:16.130
I'll go, too.

296
11:16.150 --> 11:16.820
Hey.

297
11:17.320 --> 11:18.220
Don't go.

298
11:18.520 --> 11:19.720
Grandpah, how 'bout this?

299
11:21.230 --> 11:22.230
Oh, now I'm confused.

300
11:22.250 --> 11:23.140
- Grandpa, how about this? - Mm.

301
11:23.170 --> 11:24.820
You go help Ms. Danis find the director first.

302
11:24.960 --> 11:26.300
We'll stay behind to handle those two.

303
11:26.430 --> 11:28.070
If we let them stay here,

304
11:28.220 --> 11:29.710
the tenants are bound to find out

305
11:29.730 --> 11:30.700
I'm planning to sell the dorm.

306
11:30.720 --> 11:31.430
Okye.

307
11:31.450 --> 11:32.360
Huh?!

308
11:32.520 --> 11:33.790
- Okay. - Mm.

309
11:33.810 --> 11:35.960
Hurry up. And be careful.

310
11:35.980 --> 11:37.180
If those two

311
11:37.310 --> 11:39.320
cannot find the phoenix's appendix,

312
11:39.340 --> 11:43.130
they will turn you into the phoenix's hemorrhoid.

313
11:44.330 --> 11:45.280
Just thinking about it hurts.

314
11:45.300 --> 11:45.970
What hurts?

315
11:45.990 --> 11:47.120
Hemorrhoids, obviously. Didn't you hear?

316
11:47.140 --> 11:47.700
I didn't hear anything.

317
11:48.630 --> 11:49.820
Oh, I was talking to Grandpa. I forgot.

318
11:49.840 --> 11:50.410
Oh.

319
11:52.530 --> 11:56.710
The wind shall guide me!

320
11:58.900 --> 12:02.580
The wind shall empower me!

321
12:02.830 --> 12:04.440
Whee...

322
12:05.030 --> 12:06.920
Woo...

323
12:07.420 --> 12:08.540
Whee...

324
12:08.550 --> 12:11.980
- We... - We...

325
12:12.000 --> 12:12.670
- Will... - Will...

326
12:12.690 --> 12:15.350
♫We will, we will rock you♫

327
12:15.370 --> 12:18.000
♫We will, we will rock you♫

328
12:18.020 --> 12:19.020
♫We will, we will find the appendix♫

329
12:19.040 --> 12:19.910
Hey!

330
12:20.820 --> 12:21.740
The word just fit.

331
12:21.760 --> 12:22.700
How's it going?

332
12:22.800 --> 12:24.130
Did you find the phoenix's appendix?

333
12:24.330 --> 12:26.090
If you can't find it, you can come back another day.

334
12:26.110 --> 12:26.590
This way.

335
12:26.610 --> 12:27.060
This way...

336
12:34.930 --> 12:35.930
Dohyun, what's wrong?

337
12:38.540 --> 12:39.170
Ants.

338
12:39.190 --> 12:39.990
The ants bit me.

339
12:40.130 --> 12:42.170
There... There are so many ants over there.

340
12:42.190 --> 12:43.220
- Ugh. - Ugh.

341
12:43.250 --> 12:44.890
Mr. Delta, do not fret.

342
12:44.960 --> 12:46.100
I can sense that

343
12:46.210 --> 12:49.100
the phoenix's appendix will surely make an appearance.

344
12:49.120 --> 12:49.980
- Oh. - Oh.

345
12:50.830 --> 12:51.850
Whoa!

346
12:51.870 --> 12:53.510
There are a lot of you today. What can I get you?

347
12:56.330 --> 12:57.380
- Oh! - Oh!

348
12:57.460 --> 12:58.380
The phoenix's appendix.

349
12:58.400 --> 12:59.550
Stir-fried or deep-fried?

350
12:59.580 --> 13:00.340
- Hey! - Hey!

351
13:00.360 --> 13:01.830
I sell made-to-order food,

352
13:01.850 --> 13:02.630
not foraged food.

353
13:03.010 --> 13:04.540
What do you mean, appendix?

354
13:04.560 --> 13:05.420
Dohyun,

355
13:05.930 --> 13:07.380
are you sure that's the phoenix's appendix?

356
13:07.410 --> 13:08.980
She looks more like adrenal glands to me.

357
13:09.800 --> 13:10.750
Who are these two?

358
13:11.310 --> 13:12.830
Why are you calling me adrenal glands, huh?

359
13:12.950 --> 13:14.110
Hello, I'm Delta.

360
13:14.130 --> 13:15.510
- I came here to buy... - Buy?

361
13:15.520 --> 13:17.360
Buy...food from your place.

362
13:17.390 --> 13:19.070
Red curry, chicken curry, eel curry, chu chee,

363
13:19.090 --> 13:20.300
massaman curry, stir-fried noodles, yellow curry,

364
13:20.320 --> 13:22.410
and poh...teak!

365
13:22.420 --> 13:25.060
Wow! If they're ordering this much, call me adrenal glands,

366
13:25.090 --> 13:26.960
or even a wart on my big toe.

367
13:27.550 --> 13:28.170
Just a sec.

368
13:28.190 --> 13:29.120
Please wait.

369
13:29.140 --> 13:29.740
- Yes. - Thank you.

370
13:30.030 --> 13:30.740
Mm.

371
13:33.120 --> 13:33.810
Hey,

372
13:34.340 --> 13:35.420
what are you gonna do with her?

373
13:35.440 --> 13:36.720
I'm not going to do anything to her.

374
13:36.740 --> 13:37.980
I just want to ask her to work for me.

375
13:38.320 --> 13:39.120
That is right.

376
13:39.140 --> 13:41.310
To enhance Mr. Delta's fortune and prestige,

377
13:42.020 --> 13:44.530
it is essential that someone born under the Phoenix sign

378
13:44.550 --> 13:47.370
serve as one of his subordinates, working close by his side.

379
13:47.400 --> 13:48.060
Ugh...

380
13:48.460 --> 13:49.460
- She's not going anywhere. - Mm.

381
13:49.480 --> 13:50.860
She loves her kids to death.

382
13:50.880 --> 13:51.330
That's right.

383
13:51.350 --> 13:52.770
She wouldn't leave them behind.

384
13:52.800 --> 13:53.490
Mm.

385
13:53.620 --> 13:55.120
Think she'll still be able to resist

386
13:56.240 --> 13:57.860
a house and a monthly salary of 300,000 baht?

387
13:58.510 --> 13:59.320
300,000?!

388
14:00.030 --> 14:01.100
Whoa. Uh...excuse me.

389
14:01.120 --> 14:02.230
Could you check my birth fortune, too?

390
14:02.340 --> 14:04.300
Maybe I'm the phoenix's butt hair.

391
14:04.430 --> 14:05.990
Ugh! Dax!

392
14:06.170 --> 14:06.770
What?

393
14:06.930 --> 14:07.740
Hey,

394
14:07.770 --> 14:08.780
she's not going anywhere.

395
14:08.800 --> 14:11.300
If you're offering her a house and money like that,

396
14:11.320 --> 14:12.200
she's certainly not gonna leave.

397
14:12.220 --> 14:13.070
She doesn't like rich people

398
14:13.080 --> 14:14.900
who think they can win others over with money.

399
14:14.980 --> 14:17.000
But you only ordered a few dishes,

400
14:17.230 --> 14:18.960
and she became a wart on the big toe.

401
14:20.230 --> 14:20.890
Hey,

402
14:21.520 --> 14:22.580
she was just joking.

403
14:22.720 --> 14:24.030
She wouldn't agree to that.

404
14:24.320 --> 14:25.300
How about this?

405
14:25.320 --> 14:27.210
If you really want Auntie Duang to work with you,

406
14:27.820 --> 14:29.120
I can try to persuade her.

407
14:30.040 --> 14:32.460
Because the tenants haven't come to terms

408
14:32.620 --> 14:34.120
with having to leave this dorm yet.

409
14:34.270 --> 14:36.610
And if they find out your father is gonna buy this dorm...

410
14:36.630 --> 14:38.020
Oh, that'll break their hearts.

411
14:39.630 --> 14:40.630
Is that alright with you?

412
14:41.910 --> 14:42.510
Okay.

413
14:42.620 --> 14:43.620
Dobby, Dobby,

414
14:44.050 --> 14:45.220
- come here. - What?

415
14:46.120 --> 14:47.450
How are you gonna tell this to Auntie Duang?

416
14:47.470 --> 14:49.140
Come on, I've got a way to handle this.

417
14:49.230 --> 14:50.620
Even if we sell this dorm,

418
14:50.640 --> 14:51.940
she'll have to close her place anyway.

419
14:52.420 --> 14:53.190
At least

420
14:53.210 --> 14:55.460
we could help her find a way to support herself.

421
14:56.320 --> 14:57.120
Listen,

422
14:57.140 --> 14:59.320
keep an eye on those two.

423
14:59.630 --> 15:02.510
Don't let them tell anyone about the dorm purchase,

424
15:02.710 --> 15:03.280
alright?

425
15:03.520 --> 15:04.200
Okay.

426
15:06.380 --> 15:06.910
- Oh... - Oh...

427
15:08.830 --> 15:09.960
- Okay... - Okay?

428
15:09.980 --> 15:11.750
Is that alright, Mr. Delta?

429
15:15.140 --> 15:16.220
Excuse me,

430
15:16.660 --> 15:19.110
have you seen this woman in this photo around here?

431
15:19.310 --> 15:20.530
No, I haven't.

432
15:22.440 --> 15:22.920
Watch out...

433
15:22.970 --> 15:24.360
Oh, Guard Dum.

434
15:24.380 --> 15:26.190
Why are you just pushing that cart around?

435
15:26.210 --> 15:27.840
Why aren't you helping me look for my mother?

436
15:28.020 --> 15:29.990
I'm not pushing it around for fun. I'm pushing a sleeping person.

437
15:30.660 --> 15:31.440
Whoa!

438
15:31.460 --> 15:32.190
Handyman Daeng.

439
15:33.380 --> 15:34.600
Whoa! I found her!

440
15:34.620 --> 15:36.100
I found the director!

441
15:36.120 --> 15:37.150
Where? Where is she?

442
15:37.740 --> 15:38.950
I... I found her in my dreams.

443
15:38.970 --> 15:39.660
Ugh...

444
15:39.680 --> 15:41.730
Not only are you not helping, you're being a burden.

445
15:43.920 --> 15:45.060
- Oh, oh. - Oh, be careful.

446
15:45.080 --> 15:46.500
Don't say that.

447
15:46.530 --> 15:47.790
I'm trying my best here.

448
15:48.440 --> 15:49.920
I was looking for her

449
15:50.220 --> 15:51.460
even in my dreams.

450
15:52.970 --> 15:55.320
The police haven't made any progress either.

451
15:56.740 --> 15:57.230
Let's go.

452
15:57.240 --> 15:58.560
Let's look for her together.

453
15:58.820 --> 15:59.450
- Hey! - Ow.

454
15:59.470 --> 16:00.070
Whoa.

455
16:00.230 --> 16:02.140
Why did you steal my sports car?

456
16:02.620 --> 16:03.580
What sports car?

457
16:03.600 --> 16:04.620
This!

458
16:04.740 --> 16:06.350
The Must-have sports car.

459
16:06.370 --> 16:07.690
It's the real deal.

460
16:08.540 --> 16:09.260
Hey...

461
16:09.420 --> 16:10.780
He's that madman living near our dorm.

462
16:10.810 --> 16:12.300
Madman, my foot.

463
16:12.840 --> 16:13.800
He came all the way here?

464
16:15.340 --> 16:16.650
Hello, beautiful.

465
16:16.710 --> 16:19.250
Wanna go for a ride in my sports car?

466
16:25.980 --> 16:26.620
Hey!

467
16:30.140 --> 16:32.110
That's my mother's shawl!

468
16:32.380 --> 16:32.990
Really?

469
16:33.210 --> 16:34.120
Hey, give it to me!

470
16:34.150 --> 16:34.820
Hey!

471
16:34.840 --> 16:35.460
What the heck?

472
16:35.470 --> 16:36.090
Hey!

473
16:36.110 --> 16:37.730
Don't you dare touch my car, red panda.

474
16:38.500 --> 16:39.830
Please calm down.

475
16:39.850 --> 16:42.100
We're not going to do anything to your car.

476
16:42.240 --> 16:43.180
I just want to ask...

477
16:43.200 --> 16:45.080
where did you get that shawl?

478
16:45.100 --> 16:46.410
You really wanna know?

479
16:46.930 --> 16:47.740
If you wanna know,

480
16:47.750 --> 16:49.910
why don't you come for a spin with me?

481
16:50.250 --> 16:50.910
A spin...

482
16:51.850 --> 16:52.880
Be careful, Ms. Danis.

483
16:52.890 --> 16:53.800
I remember now.

484
16:53.820 --> 16:54.850
This madman

485
16:54.870 --> 16:56.240
once chased Mr. Drip

486
16:56.330 --> 16:58.180
and hurt his leg so badly he ended up in the hospital.

487
16:58.820 --> 17:00.830
But if we find out where he got that shawl,

488
17:00.850 --> 17:02.650
it'll be easier to look for my mother.

489
17:02.670 --> 17:04.650
Hey, we're talking about a madman here.

490
17:04.670 --> 17:06.430
"Madman," my foot! I'm not crazy.

491
17:07.230 --> 17:08.329
He's not right in the head.

492
17:08.349 --> 17:09.760
Now that sounds a lot better.

493
17:11.230 --> 17:12.230
Uh...

494
17:12.380 --> 17:13.910
It's broad daylight. We'll probably be fine.

495
17:16.020 --> 17:17.690
Hey, handsome.

496
17:17.940 --> 17:19.460
Yes, beautiful?

497
17:19.490 --> 17:21.650
I want to ask you something.

498
17:21.670 --> 17:22.710
But on one condition.

499
17:22.730 --> 17:25.859
You have to come for a little ride with me.

500
17:26.740 --> 17:28.610
Right this way. I'll open the door for you.

501
17:31.660 --> 17:32.890
Is that a door or a coffin opening?

502
17:32.920 --> 17:33.820
A door, obviously.

503
17:34.940 --> 17:35.620
Hop in.

504
17:37.120 --> 17:37.660
Okay.

505
17:37.830 --> 17:38.830
Come, come.

506
17:39.220 --> 17:40.220
- Yes, thank you... - Hop in.

507
17:40.240 --> 17:41.650
Thank you.

508
17:43.450 --> 17:44.900
- Be careful, alright? - Yes.

509
17:44.930 --> 17:46.230
The seat might bounce.

510
17:48.130 --> 17:49.130
- Ow, ow! - Whoa!

511
17:49.310 --> 17:50.100
- What? - Ow, ow.

512
17:50.120 --> 17:50.960
The door caught my finger.

513
17:51.810 --> 17:53.010
Not used to a luxury car, huh?

514
17:53.980 --> 17:55.580
[The D Dorm]

515
17:56.710 --> 17:57.730
How am I gonna convince her

516
17:57.750 --> 18:00.200
to be the phoenix's appendix for Mr. Delta?

517
18:01.430 --> 18:02.600
Should I come up with something?

518
18:02.710 --> 18:03.980
What are you planning to tell her?

519
18:04.220 --> 18:05.020
I'm not.

520
18:05.720 --> 18:06.720
Huh? Who was that?

521
18:13.510 --> 18:14.200
What are you doing?

522
18:14.230 --> 18:17.010
I'm training for the HYROX competition with Dollar.

523
18:18.540 --> 18:19.430
Hope you come in first.

524
18:19.460 --> 18:20.480
- Thank you so much. - Mm...

525
18:20.500 --> 18:21.510
Hey, wait.

526
18:21.530 --> 18:21.920
Hm?

527
18:21.940 --> 18:23.650
I heard what you said earlier, Mr. Dobby.

528
18:23.670 --> 18:24.810
Are you planning to trick Auntie Duang?

529
18:24.820 --> 18:25.670
Spill the beans.

530
18:26.410 --> 18:27.430
This is between the adults.

531
18:27.770 --> 18:28.560
Stay out of it, alright?

532
18:29.520 --> 18:30.750
I can't stay out of it.

533
18:30.770 --> 18:32.940
If anything happens to Dollar's mom,

534
18:32.960 --> 18:35.910
how's he supposed to have the heart to compete in HYROX with me?

535
18:35.930 --> 18:37.470
So answer me, Mr. Dobby,

536
18:37.740 --> 18:39.700
- are you planning to trick Auntie Duang? - Hm!

537
18:39.940 --> 18:41.330
Who? Who's trying to trick me?

538
18:43.310 --> 18:44.820
No one, Auntie Duang.

539
18:45.140 --> 18:47.320
Well...my friend

540
18:47.340 --> 18:48.220
got scammed by his housemaid,

541
18:48.330 --> 18:49.700
so he's looking for a new one.

542
18:49.810 --> 18:51.500
He's offering 300,000 baht!

543
18:51.520 --> 18:52.320
300,000?!

544
18:52.340 --> 18:53.540
That's right.

545
18:53.560 --> 18:55.390
Is he looking for a housemaid or a mistress?

546
18:56.030 --> 18:56.720
Hey, Dobby.

547
18:56.730 --> 18:58.560
I may look alluring,

548
18:58.580 --> 19:00.790
but I still have my dignity.

549
19:00.810 --> 19:02.040
Oh, I think intimidating is the right word.

550
19:02.060 --> 19:03.530
Just kidding.

551
19:03.740 --> 19:04.860
It's not like that, Auntie Duang.

552
19:04.970 --> 19:06.300
He really is looking for a housemaid.

553
19:06.320 --> 19:07.510
My friend is loaded,

554
19:07.530 --> 19:09.000
and he's taken a liking to you.

555
19:09.220 --> 19:10.630
That's why he wants you

556
19:10.720 --> 19:11.910
to work with him

557
19:12.140 --> 19:13.450
and bring him good fortune.

558
19:14.220 --> 19:14.840
Whoa...

559
19:14.860 --> 19:15.580
Yes.

560
19:15.600 --> 19:16.530
That sounds interesting.

561
19:16.540 --> 19:17.270
Yeah!

562
19:18.920 --> 19:20.250
Don't fall for it yet, Auntie.

563
19:20.270 --> 19:21.850
Listen to me carefully.

564
19:21.930 --> 19:22.720
Huh?

565
19:23.510 --> 19:24.730
Oh... Whoa.

566
19:25.830 --> 19:27.780
He's using 300,000 baht to lure you in.

567
19:29.700 --> 19:30.700
There's no doubt...

568
19:31.020 --> 19:31.810
Ugh...

569
19:32.720 --> 19:33.920
He must be a scammer.

570
19:34.230 --> 19:35.630
Hm...

571
19:36.420 --> 19:37.880
He isn't!

572
19:39.940 --> 19:40.670
If he's not,

573
19:40.680 --> 19:42.310
where does he get 300,000 baht from?

574
19:42.610 --> 19:43.580
Yeah.

575
19:44.350 --> 19:45.250
I think...

576
19:45.270 --> 19:47.430
he's tricking you into selling your organs!

577
19:47.450 --> 19:48.510
Whoa...

578
19:50.020 --> 19:51.370
If you don't believe me,

579
19:51.380 --> 19:52.540
you can talk to him first.

580
19:55.660 --> 19:56.250
Let's go.

581
19:57.760 --> 19:58.550
You want to meet my friend?

582
19:58.570 --> 19:59.570
I want to see a doctor.

583
19:59.590 --> 20:00.160
Huh?

584
20:00.180 --> 20:02.580
My knees hurt. My legs can't take this anymore.

585
20:03.430 --> 20:06.330
Dobby, if you want me to talk to your friend,

586
20:06.920 --> 20:08.750
can you wait until Dollar gets back from work?

587
20:08.780 --> 20:10.880
I feel more comfortable when I have

588
20:10.900 --> 20:12.110
a cop with me.

589
20:12.130 --> 20:13.540
Come on...

590
20:13.560 --> 20:14.640
Are you gonna send Dollar

591
20:14.660 --> 20:16.490
to do aerobics in front of the scammers?

592
20:16.510 --> 20:17.860
Attention!

593
20:17.880 --> 20:19.290
Present arms!

594
20:19.580 --> 20:20.740
Okay, please follow along.

595
20:20.760 --> 20:23.730
Right, left, right, left,

596
20:23.750 --> 20:25.300
right. Ow...my back.

597
20:25.620 --> 20:27.850
I'm screwed. If Dollar comes with us,

598
20:27.870 --> 20:29.900
they'll find out I'm selling this dorm.

599
20:29.920 --> 20:31.210
What should I do?

600
20:31.710 --> 20:32.560
[DO-MUN-DRIP]

601
20:47.910 --> 20:50.460
Why does he have to look so cool just smelling coffee?

602
21:04.900 --> 21:05.820
How is that cool?

603
21:06.320 --> 21:07.650
He looks like he's sniffing glue.

604
21:08.720 --> 21:10.930
This is good stuff. It really hits the spot.

605
21:12.130 --> 21:12.910
Uh...

606
21:13.130 --> 21:13.990
Mr. Dolly,

607
21:14.710 --> 21:16.990
could you give this a sniff...

608
21:17.010 --> 21:18.570
and tell me if it's over-roasted?

609
21:19.500 --> 21:20.490
Of course.

610
21:40.990 --> 21:41.990
Whoa!

611
21:43.240 --> 21:44.740
It smells so good.

612
21:47.750 --> 21:50.660
Then...I'll order more of this next time.

613
21:53.510 --> 21:55.220
Now that that's settled.

614
21:56.250 --> 21:57.310
Who called for them?

615
22:03.730 --> 22:05.530
I have eradicated all negative energy.

616
22:13.860 --> 22:14.630
Mr. Dax,

617
22:15.120 --> 22:16.720
who are you bringing into my cafe?

618
22:16.840 --> 22:17.530
Oh,

619
22:18.040 --> 22:18.980
they're Dobby's friends.

620
22:19.260 --> 22:20.000
I brought them here for coffee.

621
22:20.980 --> 22:22.400
Why is he walking like that, though?

622
22:23.390 --> 22:24.340
Or does he have a disability?

623
22:24.360 --> 22:25.230
Silence!

624
22:25.580 --> 22:27.420
Do not look down on my ritual.

625
22:27.620 --> 22:29.850
This walk is meant to bring good fortune.

626
22:30.540 --> 22:31.580
How about some shoe lifts first?

627
22:31.930 --> 22:34.100
At this rate, you'll wear your heels right down.

628
22:34.260 --> 22:35.710
How dare you?!

629
22:36.140 --> 22:36.930
Calm down.

630
22:36.950 --> 22:38.370
Delta believes in that sort of thing,

631
22:38.390 --> 22:40.840
and Dohyun is a Korean fortune teller.

632
22:43.180 --> 22:44.990
Oh...

633
22:45.020 --> 22:46.930
He said starting off on your left foot

634
22:46.960 --> 22:48.050
would bring you good luck.

635
22:49.610 --> 22:50.610
Delta.

636
22:51.420 --> 22:53.710
No wonder you look so familiar.

637
22:53.730 --> 22:54.730
Do you remember me?

638
22:55.310 --> 22:57.500
I'm Dolly!

639
22:58.640 --> 22:59.270
Dolly...

640
23:02.360 --> 23:03.360
Dol...

641
23:03.680 --> 23:04.950
Dolly Darling?

642
23:05.380 --> 23:06.310
Yes!

643
23:06.320 --> 23:07.890
Hey, I thought you had forgotten about me,

644
23:07.910 --> 23:08.910
Delta Oppa.

645
23:10.320 --> 23:11.620
Is he your friend, Mr. Dolly?

646
23:12.030 --> 23:12.760
Yes.

647
23:12.880 --> 23:14.140
We were friends back in middle school.

648
23:15.440 --> 23:17.340
One's "Dolly Darling,"

649
23:17.630 --> 23:19.620
and the other's "Delta Oppa."

650
23:19.650 --> 23:21.110
They call each other by their nicknames.

651
23:21.140 --> 23:22.310
Are they really just friends?

652
23:24.030 --> 23:25.370
If he says they're "friends," then they're "friends."

653
23:26.060 --> 23:27.680
Why do you even want to know?

654
23:27.700 --> 23:28.700
Ugh!

655
23:28.720 --> 23:29.780
What are you even mad at me for?

656
23:31.260 --> 23:32.090
I think...

657
23:32.110 --> 23:34.330
there is still some negative energy lingering here.

658
23:34.600 --> 23:35.320
We should...

659
23:35.330 --> 23:37.670
get coffee somewhere else, Mr. Delta.

660
23:38.730 --> 23:39.360
It's alright.

661
23:40.510 --> 23:41.980
Since I'm seeing an old friend, let's get it here.

662
23:44.430 --> 23:46.450
Do Korean fortune tellers crack Thai-style jokes, too?

663
23:48.310 --> 23:48.970
I missed you.

664
24:01.850 --> 24:03.120
- Hey, handsome. - Oh...

665
24:03.150 --> 24:05.670
When are you going to tell me where you got that shawl from?

666
24:05.690 --> 24:06.690
Hey...

667
24:06.710 --> 24:08.410
I'm driving right now.

668
24:08.430 --> 24:10.220
I need to condense here.

669
24:10.240 --> 24:10.930
Concentrate.

670
24:10.950 --> 24:12.570
Yes, I need to concentrate here.

671
24:12.590 --> 24:14.600
See this? The gearshift came off.

672
24:17.730 --> 24:19.320
I've been looking everywhere for you.

673
24:19.340 --> 24:20.920
So you've been messing around with this madman, huh?

674
24:20.940 --> 24:22.670
So? What are you going to do, huh?

675
24:22.680 --> 24:24.780
Are you going to let him take you to the director?

676
24:25.130 --> 24:26.130
Ms. Danis,

677
24:26.260 --> 24:27.810
I think we should stop here.

678
24:28.110 --> 24:29.940
We're not gonna get through to him anyway.

679
24:30.220 --> 24:31.290
He won't tell us anything.

680
24:32.020 --> 24:32.850
Hey, kid.

681
24:32.870 --> 24:35.050
If you're here to sell me garlands, scram.

682
24:35.310 --> 24:36.610
I don't worship any deity

683
24:36.630 --> 24:37.860
other than...

684
24:37.950 --> 24:38.540
Other than?

685
24:38.560 --> 24:39.950
Sun Wukong.

686
24:41.630 --> 24:42.950
Let me handle this.

687
24:45.300 --> 24:46.960
You poor soul.

688
24:46.980 --> 24:47.980
Oh.

689
24:48.060 --> 24:49.780
Do you revere Son Wukong?

690
24:49.800 --> 24:50.550
That's right.

691
24:50.710 --> 24:51.920
Then you shall respect me,

692
24:51.940 --> 24:53.830
for I am greater than Son Wukong.

693
24:53.930 --> 24:54.640
And you are?

694
24:54.660 --> 24:55.660
Dad Wukong.

695
24:56.200 --> 24:57.130
You never disappoint me.

696
24:57.150 --> 24:59.760
We must hasten to find the Buddha sutrists.

697
24:59.780 --> 25:00.320
Hey!

698
25:00.340 --> 25:01.340
Buddhist sutras.

699
25:01.860 --> 25:02.750
Great Dad Wukong.

700
25:02.840 --> 25:03.440
Do speak.

701
25:03.710 --> 25:05.060
What the hell are you talking about?

702
25:05.580 --> 25:06.810
Are you crazy, red panda?

703
25:06.830 --> 25:07.710
He knows how to cut you off.

704
25:07.730 --> 25:09.000
See? He remembers.

705
25:09.020 --> 25:10.070
Hey, handsome!

706
25:10.120 --> 25:11.500
Please tell me

707
25:11.520 --> 25:13.060
where you got that shawl.

708
25:13.080 --> 25:14.800
It belongs to my mother!

709
25:14.820 --> 25:17.660
I'm looking for her!

710
25:19.870 --> 25:22.420
Oh, beautiful.

711
25:23.110 --> 25:24.440
Don't cry.

712
25:25.410 --> 25:27.780
I'll tell you the truth.

713
25:27.880 --> 25:29.130
The truth is...

714
25:30.220 --> 25:31.680
you're not my type at all.

715
25:31.840 --> 25:33.050
You're so ugly.

716
25:33.160 --> 25:35.010
Get out of my Must-have car right now.

717
25:35.030 --> 25:35.990
Get out!

718
25:37.130 --> 25:37.940
Fine.

719
25:38.830 --> 25:40.060
So, that's how you want it, huh,

720
25:40.080 --> 25:41.030
handsome?

721
25:41.050 --> 25:41.910
- Oh? - Oh, boy...

722
25:42.220 --> 25:43.330
She's gonna knock some sense into you.

723
25:43.350 --> 25:45.530
What's up, ugly?

724
25:47.220 --> 25:48.290
Battle!

725
25:49.140 --> 25:50.220
I'll sleep through this one.

726
25:51.730 --> 25:53.890
You're not gonna tell me, are you?

727
25:53.910 --> 25:56.420
I only know one word in English.

728
25:57.240 --> 25:57.750
"No."

729
26:02.220 --> 26:04.000
- Fine, then. - Whoa, whoa, whoa.

730
26:04.020 --> 26:04.770
What are you doing?

731
26:05.070 --> 26:05.980
Whoa! Hey!

732
26:06.000 --> 26:06.930
Are you gonna tell me?

733
26:06.950 --> 26:08.170
Stop doing that!

734
26:08.190 --> 26:10.410
- Don't touch my Must-have car! - Where did you get that shawl from?!

735
26:10.430 --> 26:12.020
Are you gonna tell me or not?

736
26:12.940 --> 26:14.230
Come on, spill it. Tell me!

737
26:14.250 --> 26:15.780
I'll tell you now. I'll tell you.

738
26:15.800 --> 26:17.780
Too slow! Where did you get it from?!

739
26:17.800 --> 26:20.460
I got it from an auntie wearing a yellow shirt and yellow pants.

740
26:20.480 --> 26:21.770
An auntie dressed in yellow?

741
26:21.790 --> 26:23.060
Where is she now?

742
26:24.730 --> 26:26.230
Toot-toot. Chugga-chugga-chugga.

743
26:26.250 --> 26:28.280
Toot-toot. Chugga-chugga-chugga.

744
26:28.300 --> 26:30.210
Toot-toot, toot-toot.

745
26:30.230 --> 26:33.150
Oh, I know where the director is.

746
26:33.580 --> 26:34.820
Hm, let me join in.

747
26:34.840 --> 26:36.680
We shouldn't have wasted so much time playing along with him.

748
26:36.700 --> 26:38.720
If you had broken his Must-not-have car earlier,

749
26:38.730 --> 26:39.300
we'd be on our way by now!

750
26:39.320 --> 26:40.810
- Hand it to me. - Hey, hey, stop!

751
26:40.830 --> 26:42.720
- I don't care anymore. - No, no, no, don't.

752
26:43.420 --> 26:46.120
- Here. - Now I Must-find a new car.

753
26:46.130 --> 26:47.210
You'll have to wait,

754
26:47.220 --> 26:48.540
because growing these takes time.

755
26:52.320 --> 26:53.220
Die, Bob Ross.

756
26:53.630 --> 26:54.760
I'm Bob Loss.

757
26:55.320 --> 26:56.150
Mm.

758
27:03.630 --> 27:04.630
Director!

759
27:05.820 --> 27:08.820
Director, where are you? Director!

760
27:10.210 --> 27:13.030
Director, where are you? Director.

761
27:14.220 --> 27:15.410
Director!

762
27:17.420 --> 27:18.220
Oh, found you.

763
27:18.230 --> 27:20.150
She is wearing yellow. This has to be her.

764
27:20.230 --> 27:21.000
Danis!

765
27:21.020 --> 27:22.640
Danis, the director is here!

766
27:22.730 --> 27:23.740
Danis!

767
27:23.930 --> 27:24.930
Danai!

768
27:54.200 --> 27:55.500
Gaysorn!

769
27:55.730 --> 27:56.920
Danai!

770
27:58.240 --> 27:59.940
You can see me?

771
28:02.030 --> 28:03.420
Gaysorn.

772
28:04.120 --> 28:05.120
Danai.

773
28:05.240 --> 28:05.860
Danai...

774
28:18.850 --> 28:19.500
Oh...

775
28:25.120 --> 28:26.420
Gaysorn.

776
28:34.530 --> 28:35.920
Danai.

777
28:36.630 --> 28:39.620
You have not forgotten about me.

778
28:40.520 --> 28:41.920
Neither have I.

779
28:42.520 --> 28:44.730
I never forgot about you,

780
28:45.920 --> 28:47.030
Gaysorn.

781
29:17.520 --> 29:18.310
Mother.

782
29:18.330 --> 29:19.420
Director.

783
29:21.230 --> 29:21.830
Mother.

784
29:21.850 --> 29:22.610
Director.

785
29:25.030 --> 29:26.030
Mother!

786
29:27.690 --> 29:28.270
Mother!

787
29:28.380 --> 29:29.130
Mother!!

788
29:29.810 --> 29:30.940
Mother...

789
29:30.960 --> 29:32.260
Mother, are you okay?

790
29:32.280 --> 29:33.540
Are you hurt?

791
29:33.620 --> 29:34.910
I'm alright.

792
29:34.930 --> 29:36.130
I'm fine,

793
29:36.150 --> 29:37.230
Danis, my dear friend.

794
29:38.300 --> 29:38.900
Oh.

795
29:40.820 --> 29:42.000
Oh, are they your children?

796
29:42.950 --> 29:45.660
Aww, he's so cute and chubby!

797
29:46.030 --> 29:46.920
Right?

798
29:46.940 --> 29:49.520
My little brother is the cutest in the world.

799
29:50.060 --> 29:51.770
That's right. I was only recently weaned.

800
29:51.780 --> 29:52.610
Hey!

801
29:52.620 --> 29:54.040
This isn't the time to play along with her, is it?

802
29:54.070 --> 29:55.920
Um, we'd better head back now,

803
29:55.940 --> 29:58.380
so we can let the police know we've found the director.

804
29:58.680 --> 29:59.690
Let's go, Mother.

805
29:59.710 --> 30:00.260
No, no, no.

806
30:00.270 --> 30:01.770
I'm not going anywhere. I'm staying here.

807
30:02.020 --> 30:03.500
I'm meeting my boyfriend.

808
30:03.530 --> 30:04.530
Boyfriend?

809
30:05.120 --> 30:06.380
Who is your boyfriend?

810
30:10.320 --> 30:12.200
Look. That's my boyfriend, Danai.

811
30:12.620 --> 30:13.320
Huh?

812
30:18.510 --> 30:19.730
And don't tell anyone, okay?

813
30:19.750 --> 30:20.630
He said

814
30:20.650 --> 30:23.710
he's taking me with him to Chiang Mai.

815
30:25.520 --> 30:27.010
My boyfriend, Danai!

816
30:27.540 --> 30:28.540
Did I see that right?

817
30:28.830 --> 30:30.690
That's Mr. Dobby on the TV, isn't it?

818
30:33.530 --> 30:34.500
Danai...

819
30:34.730 --> 30:36.240
that's Gramps' name.

820
30:37.320 --> 30:38.320
Don't tell me

821
30:38.530 --> 30:39.530
the director

822
30:41.230 --> 30:42.740
is Grandma Gaysorn?

823
30:48.180 --> 30:50.300
[DO-MUN-DRIP]

824
30:51.760 --> 30:53.580
Dolly Darling, you can eat garlic chives now?

825
30:54.180 --> 30:55.260
Didn't you say you hated the smell?

826
30:55.400 --> 30:57.530
Delta Oppa, you still remember that?

827
30:58.450 --> 30:59.430
Maybe because I'm older.

828
31:00.100 --> 31:01.470
Now I can eat things

829
31:01.620 --> 31:02.910
I never used to eat.

830
31:03.320 --> 31:04.830
I can even eat

831
31:05.030 --> 31:05.950
bitter melons now.

832
31:10.250 --> 31:11.380
Didn't you say you'd grown up?

833
31:11.980 --> 31:13.020
You're making a mess like a little kid.

834
31:22.220 --> 31:23.220
Mr. Delta,

835
31:23.550 --> 31:25.110
can I have some tissues?

836
31:25.310 --> 31:26.460
- Whoa! - Whoa!

837
31:26.980 --> 31:28.110
Can you wipe it off for me?

838
31:29.540 --> 31:31.310
Mm, alright.

839
31:31.720 --> 31:33.120
Jeez...what did you even eat?

840
31:33.130 --> 31:34.110
How did you make such a mess?

841
31:43.200 --> 31:44.200
Mr. Dolly,

842
31:44.940 --> 31:45.980
let me wipe it off for you.

843
31:51.520 --> 31:54.020
He wants to help, but he physically can't.

844
31:56.810 --> 31:58.180
Mr. Drip, please sit still.

845
31:58.520 --> 31:59.620
This is nothing.

846
32:05.590 --> 32:06.510
This is for you.

847
32:08.150 --> 32:09.240
Let me crack this open for you.

848
32:13.190 --> 32:13.820
Ow.

849
32:15.260 --> 32:15.970
Are you alright?

850
32:23.650 --> 32:24.790
Just kidding.

851
32:26.760 --> 32:27.550
Here.

852
32:31.570 --> 32:32.570
Thank you.

853
32:41.450 --> 32:42.340
Want some ice?

854
32:43.090 --> 32:44.950
Ugh...

855
32:44.970 --> 32:46.750
are you really his friend?

856
32:46.770 --> 32:48.670
How could you not know

857
32:48.690 --> 32:50.060
Mr. Delta likes his drink without ice?

858
32:51.130 --> 32:51.870
Oh, really?

859
32:51.890 --> 32:53.320
Then why'd you

860
32:53.340 --> 32:55.910
always get extra ice back in school?

861
32:55.930 --> 32:56.960
I got it for you.

862
32:57.380 --> 32:59.010
You'd always get grumpy

863
32:59.030 --> 32:59.990
when your drink wasn't cold.

864
33:02.260 --> 33:04.960
Ugh...

865
33:05.850 --> 33:07.080
Does your cafe have a fire extinguisher?

866
33:07.100 --> 33:08.830
Seems like an old flame is flaring up again!

867
33:10.670 --> 33:11.400
No.

868
33:12.150 --> 33:13.470
We don't use charcoal anymore.

869
33:13.490 --> 33:14.350
Pollution!

870
33:14.640 --> 33:15.750
Ugh!

871
33:16.470 --> 33:17.530
Why get angry?

872
33:19.550 --> 33:20.550
Uh...

873
33:20.660 --> 33:21.970
we're closed now.

874
33:22.760 --> 33:25.600
I'm going to have to ask everyone to head out.

875
33:26.050 --> 33:26.840
What?

876
33:27.350 --> 33:28.830
Why are you closing so early today?

877
33:32.020 --> 33:33.390
We should get going, Mr. Delta.

878
33:33.450 --> 33:35.350
We have to talk to the phoenix's appendix, too.

879
33:36.160 --> 33:37.160
Alright.

880
33:37.180 --> 33:37.750
Oh,

881
33:37.960 --> 33:38.770
let me get your Instagram.

882
33:39.710 --> 33:40.190
Alright.

883
33:42.680 --> 33:45.820
Oh, a bad omen. A bad omen!

884
33:45.840 --> 33:47.810
Bad wheel. What a terrible wheelchair!

885
33:48.500 --> 33:51.120
I sense a bad omen.

886
33:51.140 --> 33:52.260
Bad wheel!

887
33:52.280 --> 33:53.570
What a terrible wheelchair!

888
33:56.950 --> 33:57.640
Ugh!

889
33:58.830 --> 34:00.060
What's up with you two?

890
34:00.230 --> 34:01.200
Mr. Delta,

891
34:01.350 --> 34:02.090
I think...

892
34:02.110 --> 34:03.540
we should not stay here.

893
34:03.840 --> 34:05.280
We should go home.

894
34:05.300 --> 34:07.070
What about...the phoenix's appendix?

895
34:07.090 --> 34:09.900
We can let Mr. Dobby talk to her for us.

896
34:10.340 --> 34:11.210
Because...

897
34:11.230 --> 34:13.580
the restaurant upstairs is going to be torn down with the building anyway.

898
34:13.960 --> 34:15.060
I think...

899
34:15.080 --> 34:16.860
she will not have much of a choice anyway.

900
34:17.170 --> 34:18.350
Delta, what's the meaning of this?

901
34:19.840 --> 34:21.469
What is Dobby saying to Mom?

902
34:21.659 --> 34:23.150
They're demolishing this building?

903
34:23.170 --> 34:25.060
Oh, uh... Well...

904
34:26.260 --> 34:27.409
Mr. Dohyun got it wrong.

905
34:28.190 --> 34:29.870
Demolish the building? That's ridiculous!

906
34:31.050 --> 34:32.469
Delta said Auntie Duang

907
34:32.480 --> 34:34.110
looks like Lisa,

908
34:34.130 --> 34:35.130
so he asked Dobby

909
34:35.150 --> 34:37.020
to convince her to have her face deconstructed in Korea.

910
34:38.080 --> 34:38.780
Right?

911
34:38.949 --> 34:39.949
Really...?

912
34:39.969 --> 34:41.630
What's the truth, Delta?

913
34:41.750 --> 34:44.760
You said everyone in the dorm already knew it was going to be sold,

914
34:44.850 --> 34:45.940
but they just needed time to process it, though?

915
34:49.050 --> 34:49.929
But didn't Mr. Dobby say

916
34:49.940 --> 34:51.719
he wasn't selling this dorm anymore?

917
34:53.949 --> 34:55.940
Or have you two been lying to us this whole time?

918
34:57.650 --> 34:58.960
What's the truth, Mr. Dax?

919
35:00.060 --> 35:01.550
Dax...

920
35:02.480 --> 35:03.640
Dax!

921
35:05.560 --> 35:07.270
Mr. Dax, tell us the truth.

922
35:08.230 --> 35:10.160
Dax...

923
35:10.260 --> 35:11.390
Dax!

924
35:12.310 --> 35:13.200
Mr. Dax.

925
35:14.260 --> 35:15.770
I... I sense a bad omen here.

926
35:15.790 --> 35:16.790
I can sense a bad omen.

927
35:16.830 --> 35:18.030
I can sense a bad omen.

928
35:18.050 --> 35:19.150
- Come here. - Here is... Ow.

929
35:19.730 --> 35:20.510
Oh, what a bad omen!

930
35:20.520 --> 35:21.950
- Take care of him, Korean shaman. - A bad omen.

931
35:21.960 --> 35:22.710
Korean shaman.

932
35:27.100 --> 35:29.300
[The D Dorm]

933
35:29.450 --> 35:30.940
Alright, dear.

934
35:30.960 --> 35:31.960
It's okay.

935
35:32.560 --> 35:33.760
Go on, get back to work.

936
35:34.080 --> 35:35.080
Mm, mm.

937
35:35.760 --> 35:37.850
Dollar needs to collect evidence

938
35:37.870 --> 35:39.760
and bring a round table to the police station.

939
35:39.850 --> 35:40.630
Hm?

940
35:41.740 --> 35:42.610
A round table again?

941
35:42.630 --> 35:43.230
Mm.

942
35:43.250 --> 35:43.910
What case is it?

943
35:44.160 --> 35:45.500
The kids were doing drugs.

944
35:45.520 --> 35:48.140
When the police showed up, they hid the drugs in the table.

945
35:48.160 --> 35:50.170
Now Dollar has to haul it to the station for evidence.

946
35:50.180 --> 35:51.270
Whoa, this is getting out of hand.

947
35:51.360 --> 35:52.860
- I see. - Yeah.

948
35:52.880 --> 35:53.640
Dobby.

949
35:53.670 --> 35:54.310
Yes?

950
35:54.330 --> 35:56.490
Let's talk about your friend who wants to

951
35:56.510 --> 35:57.510
hire me another time.

952
35:57.530 --> 35:58.990
Hm... Let's talk about it today.

953
35:59.020 --> 36:00.650
- Ugh... - I'm right here with you.

954
36:00.670 --> 36:02.200
I won't let you get tricked.

955
36:02.270 --> 36:03.270
No need!

956
36:04.070 --> 36:05.350
Your friend has left.

957
36:05.960 --> 36:07.820
Delta told me everything.

958
36:10.260 --> 36:10.710
What?

959
36:11.780 --> 36:13.390
- Huh? - They already know you're gonna sell the dorm.

960
36:13.680 --> 36:14.420
Dax, what is it?

961
36:17.090 --> 36:18.680
- What?! Just say it. - Ugh!

962
36:18.840 --> 36:20.230
I told you I couldn't stop them.

963
36:20.950 --> 36:23.150
Now they know you're gonna sell this dorm.

964
36:23.170 --> 36:24.170
- Huh?! - Huh?

965
36:24.250 --> 36:25.120
It's true.

966
36:25.140 --> 36:26.260
How could you do this to us?

967
36:26.870 --> 36:28.160
When are you going to tell us?

968
36:28.950 --> 36:31.030
Or did you want us to have no roof over our heads first?

969
36:31.850 --> 36:34.150
You want to see Auntie Duang curled up under the footbridge,

970
36:34.160 --> 36:35.210
eating out of the trash, huh?

971
36:36.760 --> 36:38.660
So cold! I'm starving!

972
36:38.840 --> 36:39.610
Oh...

973
36:39.630 --> 36:40.690
Oh... Ugh!

974
36:40.710 --> 36:42.170
Hey, stop it,

975
36:42.390 --> 36:43.440
you fortune teller who lost to AI!

976
36:44.550 --> 36:45.550
Dobby,

977
36:45.760 --> 36:46.960
is what he said

978
36:47.540 --> 36:48.630
true?

979
36:52.750 --> 36:53.410
Yes.

980
36:55.170 --> 36:57.390
I already signed the purchase contract.

981
36:58.630 --> 37:00.750
Uh... But don't worry, everyone.

982
37:00.770 --> 37:01.770
You'll...

983
37:02.060 --> 37:03.750
receive compensation.

984
37:03.770 --> 37:05.720
Do you think we want your compensation?

985
37:05.950 --> 37:06.950
I know.

986
37:07.650 --> 37:09.460
But it's the only way I can...

987
37:09.560 --> 37:11.120
make it up to everyone.

988
37:12.960 --> 37:15.650
I'm sorry I lied to you all,

989
37:16.850 --> 37:18.910
but I had to do this.

990
37:19.160 --> 37:20.040
You had to, huh?

991
37:22.170 --> 37:23.590
What is it, then?

992
37:23.960 --> 37:24.950
Speak.

993
37:25.050 --> 37:26.050
Answer me!

994
37:26.160 --> 37:27.470
What made you do this?

995
37:27.650 --> 37:29.100
Why did you lie to us?

996
37:29.120 --> 37:29.950
Mm.

997
37:31.050 --> 37:32.640
I didn't want to lie to you.

998
37:34.020 --> 37:36.130
I have to find Grandma Gaysorn

999
37:36.460 --> 37:37.870
so Grandpa can be reincarnated.

1000
37:38.040 --> 37:39.550
Don't you dare use him as an excuse.

1001
37:39.950 --> 37:40.950
I'm not.

1002
37:41.250 --> 37:42.940
I actually can communicate with him.

1003
37:43.850 --> 37:44.730
You don't believe me, right?

1004
37:45.460 --> 37:46.070
Grandpa!

1005
37:46.850 --> 37:47.850
Grandpa!

1006
37:48.450 --> 37:49.450
Grandpa!

1007
37:49.690 --> 37:50.820
Please show yourself, Grandpa!

1008
37:50.840 --> 37:52.240
Show yourself to everyone here!

1009
37:52.370 --> 37:53.190
Grandpa!

1010
37:53.210 --> 37:54.610
Enough, you jerk!

1011
37:54.630 --> 37:55.280
Whoa!

1012
37:56.710 --> 37:58.740
I won't believe another word you say!

1013
38:02.230 --> 38:03.360
Danis. Danis.

1014
38:05.910 --> 38:07.410
Me neither!

1015
38:08.220 --> 38:09.540
Me neither!

1016
38:10.590 --> 38:11.480
I don't believe you!

1017
38:13.490 --> 38:14.340
No.

1018
38:14.540 --> 38:15.350
You don't believe him?

1019
38:15.380 --> 38:16.510
We didn't say a word.

1020
38:16.650 --> 38:17.310
Why are you just

1021
38:17.320 --> 38:19.160
standing there like Gramps' cardboard cutout? Move!

1022
38:19.460 --> 38:21.350
Let's go watch the news about the monk in our subdistrict instead.

1023
38:23.460 --> 38:24.950
- You don't believe me either? - I believe you.

1024
38:25.140 --> 38:27.010
- Thank you so much, Dax. - Are you alright, Dobby?

1025
38:27.340 --> 38:28.860
- Oh, it's not that bad. - Dobby, Dobby!

1026
38:28.890 --> 38:30.640
I met Gaysorn.

1027
38:30.850 --> 38:32.880
I finally met Gaysorn.

1028
38:32.900 --> 38:35.330
She is Danis's director.

1029
38:35.420 --> 38:36.810
I am so happy.

1030
38:36.830 --> 38:38.840
Most importantly, she is still alive.

1031
38:38.860 --> 38:41.020
She still remembers me!

1032
38:42.530 --> 38:43.860
What's wrong with your eye?

1033
38:44.110 --> 38:45.090
Eye...

1034
38:45.110 --> 38:46.880
Well, "I," your grandpa,

1035
38:46.900 --> 38:49.150
am very happy

1036
38:49.170 --> 38:51.240
because I am going to see my first love.

1037
38:51.260 --> 38:53.600
Gaysorn, Gaysorn!

1038
38:53.640 --> 38:56.650
Yay!

1039
39:03.960 --> 39:05.830
- Auntie Duang, I wanna order... Ow! - Go! Shoo!

1040
39:05.860 --> 39:07.320
- Get away! - Ow, ow!

1041
39:07.340 --> 39:09.090
He didn't want to lie to you all

1042
39:09.120 --> 39:10.160
about selling the dorm.

1043
39:10.180 --> 39:11.340
He did this

1044
39:11.360 --> 39:12.710
because he wanted to help his grandpa

1045
39:12.720 --> 39:13.990
find Grandma Gaysorn.

1046
39:14.030 --> 39:15.190
If Gramps' ghost really does exist,

1047
39:15.240 --> 39:16.070
prove it, then.

1048
39:16.080 --> 39:17.360
- Mm, mm. - Yeah.

1049
39:17.370 --> 39:18.140
Prove it.

1050
39:18.570 --> 39:19.350
Ready, Handyman Daeng?

1051
39:20.630 --> 39:21.550
Well, you'd better be.

1052
39:22.510 --> 39:23.230
You just grabbed my hand

1053
39:23.240 --> 39:24.660
without warning!

1054
39:26.140 --> 39:27.440
Can you see me now?

1055
39:32.250 --> 39:35.790
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

1056
39:35.810 --> 39:39.510
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

1057
39:42.050 --> 39:47.530
♫Every step we take has a meaning♫

1058
39:49.280 --> 39:54.240
♫No path is ever meaningless♫

1059
39:56.430 --> 40:02.570
♫As long as our hearts keep searching♫

1060
40:03.550 --> 40:08.110
♫One day, we'll find what we're yearning for♫

1061
40:08.140 --> 40:11.680
♫Walking alone is fine, but it's better when you're by my side♫

1062
40:11.700 --> 40:15.300
♫It won't be lonely when you're here to walk beside♫

1063
40:15.320 --> 40:18.840
♫Like a love that waits, waits at the D Dorm♫

1064
40:18.860 --> 40:21.140
♫Like a love that remains, remains at the dorm♫

1065
40:21.160 --> 40:28.030
♫Meaningful love and good things await on every path♫

1066
40:28.220 --> 40:34.960
♫It might not be a coincidence that we get to meet♫

1067
40:35.420 --> 40:42.510
♫There might be hidden meanings on the path beneath our feet♫

1068
40:42.530 --> 40:49.640
♫Perhaps the D Dorm is what led me to meet you♫

1069
40:49.670 --> 40:53.230
[The D Dorm]
